+### Correcting a booked visit
+
+<a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
+
+A visit that has already been booked can be corrected afterwards. Its date and its description can both be changed, and the correction replaces what was recorded rather than adding a second visit to the pet `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. A correction opens with the visit's recorded date and description already in place. It is held to the same rules as booking: a description is required, and the date must be later than today. A correction that passes returns the reader to the owner's record; one that fails is put back for another attempt with the fault named. The owner's record offers no way in to a correction, and cancelling a booked visit remains out of scope (NG-5).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when its correction is opened, then the visit's recorded date and description are shown ready to be changed.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit carries the new details and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a pet with one booked visit, when a correction to it succeeds, then the pet still has exactly one visit.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the description is named, and the visit keeps its recorded details.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the date is named, and the visit keeps its recorded details.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given an owner's record, when it is opened, then it offers no way to correct a visit.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A visit whose recorded date has already passed opens carrying that past date, and cannot be submitted until the date is moved later than today.
+2. A correction never moves a visit to a different pet.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#create-or-update-form-controllers](system-design.md#create-or-update-form-controllers) · **ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is Admitted; Cancelling Stays Out of Scope](adr/2026-08-15-non-goal-visit-correction-admitted.md)
